  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Six straight wins because the Padres refuse to fold when they're chasing.",
    "what_this_means": "Luis Campusano was the difference. Three RBIs off a lineup that produced twelve hits and converted four of fifteen RISP situations into runs. That's not wasted opportunity. That's the margin between trailing after four innings and leading by three after five. Michael King held Cleveland to three runs across six innings on eight hits, then Bradgley Rodriguez closed it out with two strikeouts. The bullpen didn't give back what King set up. The bats kept coming. Campusano drove the runners in when they arrived. This is a team that wins ugly games because it doesn't stop swinging when it's behind.",
